What is High-end Copper Foil?
High-end copper foil is a specialized, high-purity copper product manufactured through advanced electrodeposition processes to achieve exceptional uniformity, tensile strength, and surface quality. Unlike standard copper foil, it features low profile surfaces, minimal roughness, and superior electrical conductivity, making it indispensable for advanced applications. This material is primarily used in Printed Circuit Boards (PCBs), lithium-ion batteries, and high-frequency communication devices where performance and reliability are critical.
These foils are categorized by their surface treatment, such as STD (Standard), RTF (Reverse Treated Foil), VLP (Very Low Profile), and HVLP (Hyper Very Low Profile), each catering to specific technological requirements. The development of ultra-thin foils, some as thin as 4–6 micrometers, is particularly crucial for next-generation miniaturized electronics and high-density battery designs.
